Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 07:38:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 124/154] feat(peek): an off-site link from a favourite's tab
 opens the card
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ShouldAutoPeek matched the source tab's committed URL against the stored
favourite exactly. A favourite's tab has no row, so its URL stops matching
after the first move within its site, and a plain link then navigated the
tab away. A target=_blank link never reached the peek code: it became a
new tab in Browser::AddNewContents.

A tab that carries a favourite claim now counts as a peek source, and a
NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB with a gesture off a peek source's site is adopted
into the card, in AddNewContents and in OpenURLFromTab. Same-site links
keep opening tabs.

Signed-off-by: János Mikó <693558+janosmiko@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc | 23 +++++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
index f78f6549402dd..4c47c74c49f96 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser.cc
@@ -1549,11 +1549,16 @@ WebContents* Browser::OpenURLFromTab(
       atrium::MaybeOpenPeek(this, source, params.url, params.referrer)) {
     return source;  // No new WebContents/window created on this path.
   }
-  // Auto-peek - a plain cross-site link click from a pinned or favourited tab
-  // - is not hooked here and never was: a plain click emits no OpenURL IPC.
-  // It lived in a navigation throttle, which the Swift cut deleted because only
-  // Swift could say whether the source tab was pinned. A follow-up rebuilds it
-  // against the Rust core.
+  // Auto-peek for a plain click lives in AtriumPeekNavigationThrottle, since
+  // a plain click emits no OpenURL IPC. A window.open with noopener does,
+  // as NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB, so the same off-site rule applies here.
+  if (params.disposition == WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB &&
+      params.is_renderer_initiated && params.user_gesture &&
+      !params.started_from_context_menu &&
+      atrium::ShouldAutoPeek(this, source, params.url) &&
+      atrium::MaybeOpenPeek(this, source, params.url, params.referrer)) {
+    return source;
+  }
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
 
   NavigateParams nav_params(this, params.url, params.transition);
@@ -1734,7 +1739,13 @@ content::WebContents* Browser::AddNewContents(
 
   // Placed past the fullscreen branches above on purpose: a deferred or
   // inactive open must not take focus, and the card always does.
-  if (disposition == WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_POPUP &&
+  // A target=_blank link off a favourite's or pinned tab's site arrives here
+  // as NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB and takes the card too.
+  const bool off_site_link_from_peek_source =
+      disposition == WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_FOREGROUND_TAB && user_gesture &&
+      atrium::ShouldAutoPeek(this, source, target_url);
+  if ((off_site_link_from_peek_source ||
+       disposition == WindowOpenDisposition::NEW_POPUP) &&
       window_action == NavigateParams::WindowAction::kShowWindow &&
       atrium::ShouldPeekPopup(
           this, source, target_url,
